What problem we tackle with our brand or website:
For Wholesalers
They rely almost entirely on word of mouth and personal relationships to find retailers. No digital presence means they're invisible to new buyers outside their existing circle. Managing inventory is done on paper or basic Excel. Pricing is inconsistent — different retailers get different prices with no system behind it. Cash flow is a constant struggle because they extend informal credit to retailers with zero tracking.
For Retailers
Finding reliable wholesalers for a specific product means calling around, visiting markets physically, and asking friends. There's no way to compare prices across suppliers in one place. Stock availability is unknown until you call or visit. Minimum order quantities are unclear upfront. Getting credit from wholesalers depends entirely on personal trust built over years — new retailers get no access to it.
For both sides
There's very little trust between strangers. No verification system, no reviews, no dispute resolution if something goes wrong. Payments are mostly cash-based with no paper trail. Communication happens over WhatsApp and phone calls that are impossible to track or manage at scale.
The biggest underlying problem
The entire wholesale-retail relationship in Pakistan runs on personal networks built over decades. If you're outside that network — a new retailer, a wholesaler in a new city — you're essentially locked out.
This is exactly the gap your platform sits in. You're not just building a website — you're building the trust infrastructure that lets strangers do business with each other.
PakMandi — Product Context & Core Problem Statement
What is PakMandi? PakMandi is a B2B wholesale marketplace connecting Pakistani wholesalers and retailers digitally. It is built for the Pakistani market with Urdu language support, designed specifically around how traditional trade actually works in Pakistan.
The core problems we are solving:
For wholesalers — they have no digital presence and rely entirely on personal networks to find retailers. Inventory is managed on paper or basic Excel. Pricing is inconsistent with no system behind it. New retailers outside their existing circle simply cannot find them.
For retailers — finding reliable wholesalers means physically visiting markets or calling around. There is no way to compare stock availability or prices across multiple suppliers in one place. Minimum order quantities are unclear upfront. Access to supplier credit depends on years of personal trust, locking out newer or smaller retailers completely.
For both sides — the entire wholesale-retail relationship in Pakistan runs on personal networks built over decades. There is no verification system, no reviews, no dispute resolution. Payments are cash-based with no paper trail. Communication is fragmented across WhatsApp and phone calls with no central management.
Our mission: To build the trust infrastructure that allows Pakistani wholesalers and retailers to do business with strangers safely, efficiently, and digitally — breaking the dependency on closed personal networks.
Our first target market: Electronics and accessories wholesalers and retailers, starting in Mardan.
Key principles the platform must reflect: Simplicity first — our users are not tech-savvy. Urdu language is not optional, it is essential. Trust signals matter more than features. Speed of onboarding must be extremely low friction.

